From 2b693b026bd40b1606e1cf98f1898669290bf7ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retro98boy <retro98boy@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 15:40:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/18] drm/rockchip: add RK3562 VOP2 support

Describe the RK3562 display controller as a single-VP VOP2 instance with four ESMART windows connected to VP0.

Add RK3562 window and video-port data, the RK3562 overlay and interface-polarity register definitions, and the RK3562-specific overlay, layer-mixer, delay, and interface-mux programming. Reuse the RK3568-compatible VP and smart-window register layouts where the hardware matches.

Enable the existing VOP2 CSU integration for RK3562 so the VOP ACLK divider is updated from the active ACLK and VP DCLK rates during CRTC enable. Keep the SoC-specific behavior behind VOP2_FEATURE_HAS_CSU and the RK3562 vop2_ops table.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c |  30 ++
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.h |  27 ++
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop2_reg.c | 367 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 424 insertions(+)

